surprising sounds coming out of  Korogocho Celina Kumar and her fellow  musicians can transform any song into  orchestral music but ghetto classics is  more than just a unique Orchestra in one  of Nairobi's largest slums Godot  classics is my second family yeah we all  stay here like brothers and sisters yeah  so maybe if I'm bored at home and I want  to relax and have fun  I just come here growing up in Korogocho  is tough but says Saleem the worst part  is the stigma attached to it she and her  fellow musicians have discovered a way  to earn dignity and respect sometimes  how people talk you know maybe a folder  slams so you can't do anything so you  find it like it's eating me inside so  that's what the thing that I want to  change  Saleem is 18 and lives with her family  the orchestra is voluntary so she earns  money teaching music giving young people  perspectives is what organizers set out  to do even though people didn't  understand at first when we first  started everyone thought we were crazy  what's this classical music nonsense you  know as opposed to gang game you know  hip-hop or something cool groovy and so  the kids I remember our first concert  here we did some excerpts from Handel's  Messiah and we were like we could have  loved us  but the idea took off with funding from  the Kenyan Art of Music Foundation I  don't think that all the kids who are in  our program will necessarily be  first-class musicians or the best  musicians around but somebody like  Celine for instance she is extremely  talented and actually I feel it's a  shame that Celine didn't come into our  program when she was much younger  because perhaps if we had met her when  she was 8 or 9 who knows what could have  come out of this and there's still  plenty of young talent among Cora  gorgeous three hundred thousand  inhabitants Celine says ghetto classics  is a lot more than just a career  opportunity musicals enabled me like to  realize myself and know who I am and  what I want in future so at least it has  made me travel a lot and meet different  people so I think music has opened my  eyes to see and to know what I want  Celine has become a role model for  others here discipline and teamwork are  essential for any career and there is  hardly a better way to learn that in  Korogocho than through the ghetto  classics Orchestra
 

